menu "BMDS drivers"

    config BMDS_DISPLAY_AT_BOOT
        bool "Show the display from boot"
        default y if SPIRAM_SPEED_200M
        default n
        help
            At boot, set the HDMI bridge up and show display 0 at 1280x720,
            60 Hz: surface 0 (single-buffered, RGB888 in PSRAM, 2.76 MB)
            with the test picture (devplan/display.md). The DMA scans the
            surface straight from PSRAM, which needs the PSRAM at 200 MHz:
            on by default only then. 'display off' stops it.

endmenu
